{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00326",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.79,
      "end_seconds": 7.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.23,
      "text": "Hi doctor, sorry, the lift was out and I had to take the stairs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.62,
      "end_seconds": 12.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "That's alright, take a seat. Tell me why you've come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.77,
      "end_seconds": 21.9,
      "duration_seconds": 9.13,
      "text": "Doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps. She's been putting on weight over the last year, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.58,
      "end_seconds": 25.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Alright, what about sore knees, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.39,
      "end_seconds": 29.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "I mean, yeah. About three months, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.57,
      "end_seconds": 33.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Have you been feeling sleepy in the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.35,
      "end_seconds": 37.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.56,
      "end_seconds": 41.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Have you been feeling out of breath on stairs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.98,
      "end_seconds": 48.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "Mm, yes. As for feeling out of breath on stairs, pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.31,
      "end_seconds": 53.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Any chest pain, heat intolerance, increased thirst or irregular periods at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.53,
      "end_seconds": 60.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "I haven't had chest pain, heat intolerance, increased thirst or irregular periods, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.3,
      "end_seconds": 63.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Alright, has there been any palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.02,
      "end_seconds": 65.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "No, no palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 66.43,
      "end_seconds": 70.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice palpitations. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.0,
      "end_seconds": 75.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.13,
      "end_seconds": 82.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.33,
      "end_seconds": 85.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.76,
      "end_seconds": 90.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.05,
      "end_seconds": 94.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Oh, no, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.99,
      "end_seconds": 98.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.03,
      "end_seconds": 122.15,
      "duration_seconds": 22.12,
      "text": "I, I have high cholesterol. I did try to ignore it for a while. Yes, diabetes. Okay, so I have high blood pressure. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I have heart disease. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.32,
      "end_seconds": 129.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "Okay, high cholesterol, that's already on your record. Good to know. How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.47,
      "end_seconds": 137.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Well, busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.86,
      "end_seconds": 140.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.76,
      "end_seconds": 144.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Well, no, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.27,
      "end_seconds": 153.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.53,
      "end_seconds": 160.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "I take rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night. Metformin. I take it 500 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 161.04,
      "end_seconds": 169.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the metformin was 250 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.57,
      "end_seconds": 172.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Alright, I see. Is the most recent prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.29,
      "end_seconds": 182.52,
      "duration_seconds": 8.23,
      "text": "No, um, I left it at home. Amlodipine. I take it 5 milligrams, once a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.23,
      "end_seconds": 185.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.88,
      "end_seconds": 188.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "About about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.0,
      "end_seconds": 189.98,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.3,
      "end_seconds": 194.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I smoke, yes, around five a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.67,
      "end_seconds": 199.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Alright, what about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.52,
      "end_seconds": 203.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.87,
      "end_seconds": 207.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.11,
      "end_seconds": 209.01,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.85,
      "end_seconds": 226.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.25,
      "end_seconds": 231.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Just a stent put in my heart, two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 231.58,
      "end_seconds": 242.13,
      "duration_seconds": 10.55,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temp 36.4 degrees, height 186 centimetres. Pressure 109 over 74, pulse is 82 beats a minute, respiratory rate 17, weight 55 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.38,
      "end_seconds": 244.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.61,
      "end_seconds": 248.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.85,
      "end_seconds": 249.55,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.37,
      "end_seconds": 253.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Right, now bend it for me, slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.22,
      "end_seconds": 263.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Your waist measures about a hundred and four centimetres."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.48,
      "end_seconds": 282.38,
      "duration_seconds": 14.9,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Okay, so my impression is this: I think we're dealing with weight gain with a metabolic cause that needs checking at this stage. It could also be an underactive thyroid, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.73,
      "end_seconds": 287.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.08,
      "end_seconds": 305.02,
      "duration_seconds": 16.94,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with weight gain with a metabolic cause that needs checking do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been putting on weight over the last year, and no irregular periods."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.58,
      "end_seconds": 307.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.35,
      "end_seconds": 311.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.68,
      "end_seconds": 313.38,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.71,
      "end_seconds": 346.34,
      "duration_seconds": 20.63,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. I'd like to arrange a sleep study for snoring and sleepiness. I'd like to arrange a thyroid test for weight gain. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. We should do a lipid profile for metabolic risk. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.32,
      "end_seconds": 350.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Oh, sure, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.92,
      "end_seconds": 376.36,
      "duration_seconds": 24.44,
      "text": "Start with small, specific changes: smaller portions, no sugary drinks, a thirty-minute walk most days. If you smoke, this is a good moment to think about stopping, and we can help you with that. I'd like you to see a dietitian as well, and I'll write the referral. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.38,
      "end_seconds": 379.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Okay, um, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.9,
      "end_seconds": 397.4,
      "duration_seconds": 16.5,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Come back after the results are back. Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 398.4,
      "end_seconds": 403.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "So, I come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 405.15,
      "end_seconds": 409.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. So, that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 410.65,
      "end_seconds": 413.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "That's everything I wanted to ask. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.15,
      "end_seconds": 414.85,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}